// Array utilities.
//
// Fixed-size arrays `[T]` cannot cross function boundaries in v0.9.0
// (no array parameters or returns yet), so generic helpers cannot be
// written in Nusa itself. Array utilities live as builtins instead:
//
// - `len(a)` — number of elements.
// - `array_sum(a)` — sum of an `[i64]`.
// - `array_min(a)` / `array_max(a)` — extremes of an `[i64]`.
//
// ```nusa
// let numbers: [i64] = [3, 1, 2];
// print(len(numbers)); // 3
// print(array_sum(numbers)); // 6
// print(array_min(numbers)); // 1
// ```
